GAL22V10
AUDIO1

CLK IOSEL MATCH AS LDS RW RESET A1 A16 A17 A18 GND
A19 DTACK NREQ BDIR S6 S5 S4 S3 S2 S1 S0 VCC

/NREQ = /IOSEL * /MATCH * /AS * /LDS * /RW * RESET * /A16 * /A17 * /A18 * /A19
AR = NREQ
S0.R = /NREQ
S1.R = S0
S2.R = S1
S3.R = S2
S4.R = S3
S5.R = S4
S6.R = S5
BDIR = S3 * /S5 * /NREQ
DTACK.T = GND
DTACK.E = S6 * /NREQ

DESCRIPTION
SolderDemon m68k YM2149F hardware-timed write interface, r1 prototype.
Oscillator 1.8432 MHz. S2 captures data, S3 starts BDIR, S5 stops it,
S6 acknowledges. BC1 is grounded and BC2 is wired directly to bus A1.
NREQ is an inverted full-select term feeding the single-product AR.
A2-A7 are intentionally ignored: the card reserves F00100-F001FF.
Only LDS byte writes are acknowledged. Program as ATF22V10C; disable
power-down option. Do not program an ATF16V8 or substitute its fuse map.
